        "title": "Hallmarks and Standards - Karat, Fineness, Assay Offices",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Hallmarking is the world's oldest consumer protection system. English gold and silver hallmarking dates to 1300 CE — predating virtually every modern consumer protection framework by 600 years. The problem it solves is fundamental: precious metals are invisible in alloy form — you cannot see that \"gold\" is 58.5% Au without assaying it."
    },
